1119
00:50:26,433 --> 00:50:27,366
That's so stingy.

1120
00:50:29,500 --> 00:50:31,400
There isn't even
a proper face shot of Tao.

1121
00:50:31,433 --> 00:50:32,533
[Only has eyes for Tao.]

1122
00:50:32,533 --> 00:50:33,566
Why?

1123
00:50:33,600 --> 00:50:34,866
Give me more.

1124
00:50:38,233 --> 00:50:39,766
What?

1125
00:50:39,800 --> 00:50:41,066
[Complains as soon as he steps out.]
No front shot of Tao.

1126
00:50:41,066 --> 00:50:42,300
The other two look better.

1127
00:50:42,300 --> 00:50:43,733
Mine was the aquarium one.

1128
00:50:43,733 --> 00:50:44,633
Tao has no front shot.

1129
00:50:45,200 --> 00:50:46,300
He's looking at Autumn.

1130
00:50:46,300 --> 00:50:47,433
Isn't yours the same?

1131
00:50:47,466 --> 00:50:49,566
He was looking right at her.

1132
00:50:49,600 --> 00:50:50,833
Exactly.

1133
00:50:51,333 --> 00:50:52,266
She's smiling.

1134
00:50:52,866 --> 00:50:53,966
[Mysterious Tao]
Tao has no front shot.

1135
00:50:54,000 --> 00:50:54,700
So boring.

1136
00:50:54,900 --> 00:50:56,800
We seriously can't even
spend these points.

1137
00:50:56,833 --> 00:50:57,933
Yeah. Just grab these two.

1138
00:50:57,933 --> 00:50:58,833
And one more.

1139
00:50:58,866 --> 00:51:00,000
Let's splurge.

1140
00:51:00,033 --> 00:51:01,033
Stuff we never dared to take.

1141
00:51:01,033 --> 00:51:02,700
Grab whatever.

1142
00:51:02,700 --> 00:51:04,133
Water gun?

1143
00:51:04,466 --> 00:51:05,800
Pan Xiaoyi.

1144
00:51:05,833 --> 00:51:07,433
[Pan Xiaoyi's Survival Points: 4]
You can only redeem two items

1145
00:51:07,433 --> 00:51:08,800
[Pan Xiaoyi's Survival Points: 4]
with your survival points.

1146
00:51:08,900 --> 00:51:10,133
[Holding it together]

1147
00:51:11,066 --> 00:51:12,500
It's fine. We'll carry things together.

1148
00:51:12,500 --> 00:51:12,933
I just took these two.

1149
00:51:12,933 --> 00:51:15,533
No, Duanduan said...

1150
00:51:15,533 --> 00:51:16,733
Duanduan said,

1151
00:51:17,266 --> 00:51:18,300
I should rely on her.

1152
00:51:18,300 --> 00:51:19,400
[Island of Affection's
No. 2 Soft-life King]

1153
00:51:19,433 --> 00:51:20,533
So we're grabbing things together.

1154
00:51:20,533 --> 00:51:22,066
[Then let's grab it all together.]
Alright, keep choosing.

1155
00:51:22,100 --> 00:51:23,333
Thanks. Appreciate it.

1156
00:51:23,333 --> 00:51:24,366
What else?

1157
00:51:24,400 --> 00:51:25,533
Honestly, nothing.

1158
00:51:25,533 --> 00:51:26,633
Want that one?

1159
00:51:26,666 --> 00:51:28,000
Fried Cracker Balls?

1160
00:51:28,033 --> 00:51:28,466
Take it.

1161
00:51:28,466 --> 00:51:28,800
You take it.

1162
00:51:28,833 --> 00:51:30,266
I'll grab it.

1163
00:51:30,266 --> 00:51:31,800
We're done.

1164
00:51:31,833 --> 00:51:33,066
Let me show you.

1165
00:51:33,066 --> 00:51:35,300
[Showing Off]

1166
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:42,733
[Struggles of Being the Island's Richest]
There's nowhere to spend these points.

1167
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:44,033
Milk.

1168
00:51:45,533 --> 00:51:46,533
Sprite.

1169
00:51:48,266 --> 00:51:49,900
Might as well clear the shelf.

1170
00:51:50,000 --> 00:51:53,900
[All Cleared Out]

1171
00:51:54,900 --> 00:51:56,100
Help me.

1172
00:52:02,300 --> 00:52:04,033
I'll carry these myself.

1173
00:52:05,933 --> 00:52:06,933
You're tiny.

1174
00:52:06,933 --> 00:52:08,166
You'll get buried under all that.

1175
00:52:09,433 --> 00:52:10,866
And this.

1176
00:52:14,700 --> 00:52:18,000
The Supply Station of Affection
is now closed.

1177
00:52:33,200 --> 00:52:35,400
Nice and cool.

1178
00:52:42,600 --> 00:52:45,033
[Weren't you dieting?]

1179
00:52:45,033 --> 00:52:46,466
I opened it without thinking.

1180
00:52:46,466 --> 00:52:47,933
Didn't even realize it.

1181
00:52:47,933 --> 00:52:49,366
You're not supposed to eat it today.

1182
00:52:49,733 --> 00:52:50,066
What now?

1183
00:52:50,100 --> 00:52:51,200
I'll just eat one.

1184
00:52:51,233 --> 00:52:51,566
It's already open.

1185
00:52:51,600 --> 00:52:52,666
[It's already opened anyway.]
Have one of each.

1186
00:52:52,666 --> 00:52:54,333
Why are you staring at me?

1187
00:52:54,333 --> 00:52:55,166
You're embarrassing me.

1188
00:52:56,333 --> 00:52:58,533
Oh, I'm sneaking food again.

1189
00:53:00,633 --> 00:53:01,633
Ripped it open in one go.

1190
00:53:03,400 --> 00:53:04,800
Why am I so quick?

1191
00:53:06,333 --> 00:53:07,200
Just eat. It's fine.

1192
00:53:09,800 --> 00:53:11,000
I've done my part.

1193
00:53:13,200 --> 00:53:14,433
So annoying.

1194
00:53:14,433 --> 00:53:16,700
I miss day-one Huihui.

1195
00:53:16,700 --> 00:53:18,033
I didn't eat anything that first day.

1196
00:53:19,133 --> 00:53:20,233
You were scared to eat then.

1197
00:53:20,266 --> 00:53:20,700
Now you're eating nonstop.

1198
00:53:20,700 --> 00:53:21,966
I wasn't in the mood.

1199
00:53:22,266 --> 00:53:23,733
I wasn't in the mood for days.

1200
00:53:23,733 --> 00:53:25,466
Well, I've been eating fine.

1201
00:53:26,066 --> 00:53:27,266
Nothing stops you from eating.

1202
00:53:28,066 --> 00:53:30,866
[Prime Time
for Growing Up]

1203
00:53:30,900 --> 00:53:31,800
Weren't you gonna change?

1204
00:53:31,833 --> 00:53:33,533
Weren't you going
for the cool, aloof vibe?

1205
00:53:33,533 --> 00:53:34,333
Too lazy now.

1206
00:53:34,333 --> 00:53:35,200
See?

1207
00:53:35,233 --> 00:53:36,833
You should join our team.

1208
00:53:38,700 --> 00:53:40,700
Come on, I wanna duke it out with you.

1209
00:53:40,700 --> 00:53:42,300
[Still Heated from Afternoon's Debate]
I want a showdown.

1210
00:53:42,300 --> 00:53:43,200
What was the first question?

1211
00:53:45,133 --> 00:53:46,000
Regret.

1212
00:53:48,233 --> 00:53:50,666
[Debate on the Island]
Pro: Never being together is sadder.

1213
00:53:50,666 --> 00:53:53,600
Con: Ending apart is sadder.

1214
00:53:53,633 --> 00:53:54,700
Ending apart hurts more.

1215
00:53:54,700 --> 00:53:56,133
Because

1216
00:53:56,133 --> 00:53:58,166
the time we spent together

1217
00:53:58,200 --> 00:53:59,533
can't be changed.

1218
00:53:59,533 --> 00:54:02,133
And it can't be redone.

1219
00:54:02,133 --> 00:54:04,233
If you factor all that in,

1220
00:54:04,266 --> 00:54:05,566
does that mean

1221
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:07,833
you weigh the pros and cons
before falling in love?

1222
00:54:07,833 --> 00:54:10,166
Then what's the point
of "fighting for love"?

1223
00:54:10,200 --> 00:54:11,300
Over.

1224
00:54:11,300 --> 00:54:12,233
Hits hard.

1225
00:54:12,266 --> 00:54:13,300
What do you mean?

1226
00:54:15,266 --> 00:54:17,800
Would you still start something
with your first love?

1227
00:54:17,833 --> 00:54:19,300
If you went back?

1228
00:54:19,300 --> 00:54:20,033
[Would still choose]
Yeah, I would.

1229
00:54:20,033 --> 00:54:20,766
[to be together.]
Yeah, I would.

1230
00:54:20,800 --> 00:54:22,533
See? You'd still choose to be together.

1231
00:54:22,533 --> 00:54:23,866
Even if it won't last.

1232
00:54:23,900 --> 00:54:25,533
Yeah. So it's sad.

1233
00:54:25,533 --> 00:54:26,233
Regret's regret.

1234
00:54:26,266 --> 00:54:26,900
But if I had another chance,

1235
00:54:26,900 --> 00:54:28,600
I'd still choose it.

1236
00:54:28,633 --> 00:54:30,166
Wait. That's the pro side.

1237
00:54:32,700 --> 00:54:34,800
On the con side,

1238
00:54:34,833 --> 00:54:37,433
knowing it wouldn't last

1239
00:54:37,433 --> 00:54:39,033
and you'd still end up single,

1240
00:54:39,033 --> 00:54:41,100
you wouldn't have started.

1241
00:54:41,100 --> 00:54:41,966
That's the con argument.

1242
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:42,666
The pro side is...

1243
00:54:42,666 --> 00:54:43,500
You care about the journey.

1244
00:54:43,500 --> 00:54:43,933
You want to experience

1245
00:54:43,933 --> 00:54:44,733
everything you shared.

1246
00:54:49,533 --> 00:54:50,966
What are you saying?

1247
00:54:51,000 --> 00:54:51,500
I don't get it.

1248
00:54:54,200 --> 00:54:56,600
[How to talk to girls the right way:]
When you talk to a woman,

1249
00:54:56,600 --> 00:54:58,166
[Mr. Pan's class is in session]
take care of her feelings

1250
00:54:58,166 --> 00:54:59,400
[Mr. Pan's class is in session]
and her hunger first.

1251
00:54:59,400 --> 00:55:01,700
Then use logic.

1252
00:55:02,133 --> 00:55:04,033
Don't reason with her

1253
00:55:04,066 --> 00:55:04,933
while she's eating.

1254
00:55:04,933 --> 00:55:05,633
No.

1255
00:55:05,666 --> 00:55:06,666
She'll just say...

1256
00:55:08,300 --> 00:55:09,133
You're right.

1257
00:55:11,266 --> 00:55:12,933
Anyway, being together but not lasting

1258
00:55:12,933 --> 00:55:13,400
feels more regretful.

1259
00:55:13,466 --> 00:55:14,566
[Not ending up together hurts]

1260
00:55:15,433 --> 00:55:16,700
Being together...

1261
00:55:16,700 --> 00:55:17,133
Yeah.

1262
00:55:17,133 --> 00:55:18,166
Then you're pro side.

1263
00:55:18,500 --> 00:55:19,033
Con side.

1264
00:55:19,066 --> 00:55:21,400
Pro is never being together.

1265
00:55:21,433 --> 00:55:25,100
Pro says
never being together hurts more.

1266
00:55:25,100 --> 00:55:25,900
More regret.

1267
00:55:25,900 --> 00:55:26,233
Right.

1268
00:55:26,266 --> 00:55:27,600
[Never being together hurts even more.]
So you support being together.

1269
00:55:29,800 --> 00:55:30,933
What are you even saying?

1270
00:55:30,933 --> 00:55:32,200
One says never being together

1271
00:55:32,233 --> 00:55:32,666
hurts more.

1272
00:55:32,666 --> 00:55:35,000
The other says it's worse
to get together and then break up.

1273
00:55:35,033 --> 00:55:35,900
Which one do you agree with?

1274
00:55:35,900 --> 00:55:37,100
I'm team "breaking up

1275
00:55:37,100 --> 00:55:37,400
hurts more".

1276
00:55:37,433 --> 00:55:38,833
Then you're on our side.

1277
00:55:38,833 --> 00:55:40,100
What? I thought that was the con side.

1278
00:55:42,133 --> 00:55:43,000
Yours is the pro side.

1279
00:55:43,033 --> 00:55:44,500
Regretting never being together.

1280
00:55:44,500 --> 00:55:47,433
Right. The pro side thinks
never being together hurts more.

1281
00:55:47,466 --> 00:55:47,966
Yeah.

1282
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:48,700
So the pro side...

1283
00:55:48,700 --> 00:55:50,100
I don't pick that.

1284
00:55:50,100 --> 00:55:50,933
[Fired Up]
So the pro side

1285
00:55:50,933 --> 00:55:52,133
[Fired Up]
would choose to be together.

1286
00:55:52,133 --> 00:55:53,833
No, it's about which regret is bigger.

1287
00:55:56,066 --> 00:55:57,600
[So fired up he stood right up.]
He doesn't get me.

1288
00:55:57,633 --> 00:55:58,100
I get her.

1289
00:55:58,100 --> 00:55:58,800
Where is...?

1290
00:55:58,833 --> 00:55:59,766
No.

1291
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:01,466
You misunderstood me.

1292
00:56:01,466 --> 00:56:02,700
I honestly think breaking up

1293
00:56:02,700 --> 00:56:04,000
hurts more.

1294
00:56:04,033 --> 00:56:04,733
That's all I meant.

1295
00:56:04,733 --> 00:56:06,666
So you'd choose not to get together.

1296
00:56:06,700 --> 00:56:08,166
So you'd choose not to get together.

1297
00:56:11,100 --> 00:56:12,500
You think that's the bigger regret?

1298
00:56:12,500 --> 00:56:14,400
[Still Arguing]
So you avoid what hurts more.

1299
00:56:14,433 --> 00:56:15,266
I'm done talking.

1300
00:56:15,266 --> 00:56:16,100
You're driving me crazy.

1301
00:56:16,100 --> 00:56:16,366
Sit.

1302
00:56:17,866 --> 00:56:18,200
Sit.

1303
00:56:20,233 --> 00:56:21,133
You sit.

1304
00:56:21,133 --> 00:56:21,533
Sit down.

1305
00:56:22,733 --> 00:56:23,466
[Doing As Told]
We're done.

1306
00:56:23,500 --> 00:56:24,566
You're not getting it.

1307
00:56:24,600 --> 00:56:25,700
I do get it.

1308
00:56:27,200 --> 00:56:28,133
You really don't.

1309
00:56:28,133 --> 00:56:29,166
It's just this question...

1310
00:56:29,200 --> 00:56:30,033
We see it differently.

1311
00:56:30,033 --> 00:56:31,166
[Different Viewpoints]

1312
00:56:31,266 --> 00:56:33,133
We're not aligned.

1313
00:56:33,133 --> 00:56:34,566
It's not about the question.

1314
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:35,100
Stop talking.

1315
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:35,900
End of discussion.

1316
00:56:39,200 --> 00:56:40,633
If we keep going, we'll start fighting.

1317
00:56:40,633 --> 00:56:41,366
See?

1318
00:56:42,500 --> 00:56:44,100
One more word and it's over.

1319
00:56:46,666 --> 00:56:48,266
What are you staring at?

1320
00:56:50,800 --> 00:56:52,200
[More Staring]

1321
00:56:53,100 --> 00:56:55,833
[Grade-school Bickering]

1322
00:56:55,866 --> 00:56:57,266
Honestly,

1323
00:56:57,266 --> 00:56:58,100
everyone had a point.

1324
00:56:58,100 --> 00:56:59,600
We just have different stances,

1325
00:56:59,633 --> 00:57:00,166
attitudes,

1326
00:57:00,200 --> 00:57:02,033
and life experiences.

1327
00:57:08,666 --> 00:57:09,733
You're changing?

1328
00:57:09,733 --> 00:57:10,966
[Get Out]
You.

1329
00:57:11,000 --> 00:57:12,000
Why?

1330
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:12,600
No reason.

1331
00:57:13,800 --> 00:57:14,466
What are you doing?

1332
00:57:14,466 --> 00:57:15,566
My own thing.

1333
00:57:15,600 --> 00:57:16,533
Just tell me, and I'll go.

1334
00:57:16,533 --> 00:57:19,133
I'm tidying my room.

1335
00:57:19,133 --> 00:57:20,233
Why can't I stay?

1336
00:57:20,266 --> 00:57:21,466
Why would you stay while I tidy?

1337
00:57:21,466 --> 00:57:22,866
Tell me what you're doing.

1338
00:57:22,866 --> 00:57:24,333
Why do I owe you an explanation?

1339
00:57:24,333 --> 00:57:25,166
Say it, and I'll go.

1340
00:57:25,200 --> 00:57:25,500
Copying your attitude.

1341
00:57:25,500 --> 00:57:27,000
Changing.

1342
00:57:27,033 --> 00:57:28,566
Why?

1343
00:57:28,600 --> 00:57:30,200
Why do you care?

1344
00:57:31,800 --> 00:57:32,466
How long?

1345
00:57:33,666 --> 00:57:35,533
Hmm. Maybe until ten.

1346
00:57:35,700 --> 00:57:36,933
[Current Beijing Time]

1347
00:57:36,933 --> 00:57:38,366
What are you doing?

1348
00:57:38,400 --> 00:57:41,000
Nothing. I just want to lie down.

1349
00:57:41,000 --> 00:57:42,533
Take a nap.

1350
00:57:42,533 --> 00:57:43,266
Fine.

1351
00:57:43,300 --> 00:57:43,900
You're hiding something.

1352
00:57:43,900 --> 00:57:45,100
I'm napping.

1353
00:57:45,100 --> 00:57:46,100
You're hiding something.

1354
00:57:46,100 --> 00:57:47,500
Look who grew up.

1355
00:57:47,500 --> 00:57:48,766
I don't want to talk right now.

1356
00:58:01,933 --> 00:58:03,200
Do your thing. I'm leaving.

1357
00:58:10,033 --> 00:58:11,366
My hair...

1358
00:58:24,133 --> 00:58:26,966
[Preparing the Last-day Gift]

1359
00:58:32,266 --> 00:58:33,600
I'm team "breaking up hurts more".

1360
00:58:33,633 --> 00:58:35,500
Then you're on our side.

1361
00:58:35,500 --> 00:58:36,166
I'm done talking.

1362
00:58:36,200 --> 00:58:37,000
You're driving me crazy.

1363
00:58:37,000 --> 00:58:37,866
Sit.

1364
00:58:37,866 --> 00:58:38,166
The question...

1365
00:58:38,200 --> 00:58:38,700
Stop talking.

1366
00:58:38,700 --> 00:58:39,766
End of discussion.

1367
00:58:50,866 --> 00:58:53,166
I process my emotions internally.

1368
00:58:53,200 --> 00:58:54,300
I'll express them,

1369
00:58:54,300 --> 00:58:55,833
but I need the other person

1370
00:58:55,866 --> 00:58:57,766
to actually care.

1371
00:58:57,800 --> 00:58:59,466
Fine. I'll ask first.

1372
00:59:02,833 --> 00:59:03,466
Who?

1373
00:59:07,000 --> 00:59:08,033
Duanduan.

1374
00:59:08,033 --> 00:59:08,900
Coming.

1375
00:59:10,433 --> 00:59:11,100
Hello.

1376
00:59:13,500 --> 00:59:14,766
Why do you look taller?

1377
00:59:15,700 --> 00:59:16,800
[Standing Still]

1378
00:59:16,833 --> 00:59:18,666
I've always been tall.

1379
00:59:18,666 --> 00:59:19,766
True.

1380
00:59:19,800 --> 00:59:20,666
Duanduan's always

1381
00:59:20,666 --> 00:59:23,200
super tall.

1382
00:59:23,233 --> 00:59:23,866
I'm freezing.

1383
00:59:25,266 --> 00:59:27,366
Grab a blanket. Need one?

1384
00:59:27,400 --> 00:59:28,633
No.

1385
00:59:28,633 --> 00:59:29,566
You don't want one?

1386
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:30,400
I do.

1387
00:59:31,533 --> 00:59:33,033
I'll wrap up.

1388
00:59:33,066 --> 00:59:35,866
Ugh, that cookie's calling me again.

1389
00:59:35,866 --> 00:59:36,800
Then eat it.

1390
00:59:36,833 --> 00:59:37,533
How much have you had today?

1391
00:59:37,933 --> 00:59:39,666
[Tucking in Tight]

1392
00:59:40,100 --> 00:59:40,733
I want that one.

1393
00:59:42,333 --> 00:59:45,566
Food boosts my mood.

1394
00:59:45,600 --> 00:59:46,933
Detoxes me.

1395
00:59:46,933 --> 00:59:48,633
And de-stresses me.

1396
00:59:48,666 --> 00:59:50,133
What mood exactly?

1397
00:59:50,133 --> 00:59:51,666
My anger.

1398
00:59:51,700 --> 00:59:52,800
Your anger?

1399
00:59:52,833 --> 00:59:53,733
Give it.

1400
00:59:53,733 --> 00:59:54,333
I'm eating it.

1401
00:59:54,333 --> 00:59:54,833
You're not.

1402
00:59:54,866 --> 00:59:55,866
Not even one.

1403
00:59:55,866 --> 00:59:56,400
I'd really get mad.

1404
00:59:56,433 --> 00:59:57,533
Fine, I won't.

1405
00:59:57,533 --> 00:59:57,766
Here.

1406
01:00:09,066 --> 01:00:09,800
Why'd you come to me?

1407
01:00:12,733 --> 01:00:13,266
To see if you're mad.

1408
01:00:14,700 --> 01:00:15,433
I'm not.

1409
01:00:17,300 --> 01:00:19,133
You're already stress eating.

1410
01:00:19,133 --> 01:00:20,966
Trying to calm down.

1411
01:00:21,000 --> 01:00:23,133
Barely holding it in.

1412
01:00:23,133 --> 01:00:24,933
I'm kinda freaking out.

1413
01:00:25,933 --> 01:00:26,400
Feels just like

1414
01:00:26,433 --> 01:00:28,166
day one on the island,

1415
01:00:28,200 --> 01:00:28,900
same nerves.

1416
01:00:31,733 --> 01:00:32,666
Is it obvious?

1417
01:00:36,866 --> 01:00:37,900
A bit.

1418
01:00:37,900 --> 01:00:38,233
No.

1419
01:00:38,266 --> 01:00:40,533
Not super obvious.

1420
01:00:40,533 --> 01:00:44,466
But it feels tense, you know?

1421
01:00:46,000 --> 01:00:49,200
[Holding Back A Laugh]

1422
01:00:50,133 --> 01:00:51,166
Earlier...

1423
01:00:53,700 --> 01:00:55,766
I was so fired up.

1424
01:00:59,700 --> 01:01:00,966
I didn't even notice.

1425
01:01:01,000 --> 01:01:02,466
My brain was running through

1426
01:01:03,100 --> 01:01:04,433
the process, the outcome, everything.

1427
01:01:06,866 --> 01:01:08,100
I was confused

1428
01:01:08,100 --> 01:01:10,166
when you suddenly told me to leave.

1429
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:11,000
I don't mind

1430
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:12,600
you changing.

1431
01:01:12,600 --> 01:01:13,866
I was writing.

1432
01:01:13,866 --> 01:01:15,133
Then suddenly,

1433
01:01:15,133 --> 01:01:16,466
something felt off.

1434
01:01:20,200 --> 01:01:23,100
Don't smile like that.

1435
01:01:25,333 --> 01:01:26,666
You were smiling so brightly before.

1436
01:01:26,700 --> 01:01:28,533
Now your smile is scary.

1437
01:01:31,300 --> 01:01:32,433
Stop smiling.

1438
01:01:34,266 --> 01:01:35,566
Seriously, stop.

1439
01:01:35,600 --> 01:01:38,066
I'm putting pressure.

1440
01:01:38,066 --> 01:01:39,666
That's full Duanduan mode.

1441
01:01:41,433 --> 01:01:42,566
I apologize.

1442
01:01:42,733 --> 01:01:43,966
[Pan Apologizes]

1443
01:01:44,000 --> 01:01:48,333
I was probably too harsh earlier.

1444
01:01:48,333 --> 01:01:51,466
I wasn't thinking.

1445
01:01:51,500 --> 01:01:53,300
I was talking and arguing
without listening.

1446
01:01:55,400 --> 01:01:55,933
And

1447
01:01:57,666 --> 01:01:58,733
I want to apologize.

1448
01:01:59,933 --> 01:02:00,766
Not accepting it.

1449
01:02:00,800 --> 01:02:01,300
Not accepting it.

1450
01:02:05,500 --> 01:02:09,166
Okay. I'll keep trying.

1451
01:02:09,200 --> 01:02:10,466
[Keeps Trying]

1452
01:02:10,466 --> 01:02:12,666
It's not that easy.

1453
01:02:12,666 --> 01:02:14,066
Just talk to me a bit.

1454
01:02:16,700 --> 01:02:18,500
If apologies solved everything,

1455
01:02:18,500 --> 01:02:20,800
why do couples fight so much? Right?

1456
01:02:24,400 --> 01:02:25,000
Don't roll your eyes.

1457
01:02:27,133 --> 01:02:29,733
I really wasn't thinking.

1458
01:02:29,733 --> 01:02:30,833
I was fired up.

1459
01:02:30,866 --> 01:02:32,800
Didn't watch my tone.

1460
01:02:32,833 --> 01:02:35,266
I acted without thinking,
all careless and rash.

1461
01:02:35,266 --> 01:02:39,133
Probably said hurtful things too.

1462
01:02:39,133 --> 01:02:40,133
Stuff like that really scares me.

1463
01:02:40,133 --> 01:02:41,866
Same in relationships.

1464
01:02:41,900 --> 01:02:42,733
I've got flaws.

1465
01:02:42,733 --> 01:02:44,366
But I'll change.

1466
01:02:44,400 --> 01:02:44,933
Bit by bit.

1467
01:02:49,266 --> 01:02:50,533
Got it.

1468
01:02:50,533 --> 01:02:51,600
Got it.

1469
01:02:51,633 --> 01:02:52,233
Got it?

1470
01:02:53,533 --> 01:02:54,566
Okay. As long as you know.

1471
01:02:54,600 --> 01:02:56,000
Forgiving is another matter.

1472
01:02:56,000 --> 01:02:57,133
I'll keep trying.

1473
01:02:57,133 --> 01:02:58,666
Knowing that already makes me happy.

1474
01:02:58,700 --> 01:02:59,366
I'm satisfied.

1475
01:02:59,400 --> 01:03:01,300
I take the win.

1476
01:03:01,300 --> 01:03:01,766
Really.

1477
01:03:16,933 --> 01:03:19,066
[When love feels thin,
we learn to breathe together.]

1478
01:03:19,100 --> 01:03:22,200
Swim until the ocean turns blue.

1479
01:03:27,400 --> 01:03:28,333
We leave tomorrow.

1480
01:03:29,600 --> 01:03:30,733
Last night.

1481
01:03:30,733 --> 01:03:32,666
Yeah. No more chances

1482
01:03:32,700 --> 01:03:33,833
for a beach walk or something.

1483
01:03:36,300 --> 01:03:37,500
Our last night.

1484
01:03:39,733 --> 01:03:40,933
Are you nervous about tomorrow?

1485
01:03:41,200 --> 01:03:42,933
[Nervous for tomorrow?]

1486
01:03:43,933 --> 01:03:44,600
Yeah.

1487
01:03:44,633 --> 01:03:46,033
How could I not be?

1488
01:03:46,033 --> 01:03:46,966
Why?

1489
01:03:50,266 --> 01:03:51,100
Because it's tomorrow.

1490
01:03:52,533 --> 01:03:53,433
Are you nervous?

1491
01:03:53,466 --> 01:03:54,400
No.

1492
01:03:54,433 --> 01:03:56,433
Good then.

1493
01:03:56,433 --> 01:03:57,666
I know what I'll do.

1494
01:03:57,666 --> 01:03:58,500
You already know?

1495
01:03:59,900 --> 01:04:00,300
Nice.

1496
01:04:05,333 --> 01:04:06,366
Not nervous at all?

1497
01:04:08,266 --> 01:04:09,966
Maybe tomorrow I will be.

1498
01:04:11,666 --> 01:04:13,700
What makes you nervous?

1499
01:04:13,700 --> 01:04:15,033
I don't know.

1500
01:04:16,333 --> 01:04:17,366
About what?

1501
01:04:23,100 --> 01:04:24,733
Whether I should just say it outright.

1502
01:04:26,200 --> 01:04:29,066
I've gotten
kind of introverted lately, bro.

1503
01:04:30,833 --> 01:04:32,066
Really, I have.

1504
01:04:35,000 --> 01:04:37,700
We'll see tomorrow.

1505
01:04:39,300 --> 01:04:40,166
See how it goes.

1506
01:04:41,700 --> 01:04:43,800
Don't forget me when you leave.

1507
01:04:46,900 --> 01:04:48,633
You're hard to forget.

1508
01:04:48,666 --> 01:04:50,366
You're hard to forget.

1509
01:04:50,400 --> 01:04:51,700
Unforgettable?

1510
01:04:51,700 --> 01:04:52,533
Good.

1511
01:04:52,533 --> 01:04:53,866
You talk too much.

1512
01:04:53,900 --> 01:04:55,333
Okay. Unforgettable works.

1513
01:04:55,333 --> 01:04:56,066
I'm not nervous anymore.

1514
01:05:03,300 --> 01:05:04,000
This is fun.

1515
01:05:04,033 --> 01:05:06,766
We've been doing this
for over ten days now.

1516
01:05:06,800 --> 01:05:07,433
All good memories.

1517
01:05:08,933 --> 01:05:11,000
Yeah. I'll post on Moments when I'm back.

1518
01:05:13,000 --> 01:05:14,733
Post what? What do you think I'll post?

1519
01:05:14,733 --> 01:05:16,800
Post a picture of me.

1520
01:05:19,266 --> 01:05:20,500
Post you?

1521
01:05:22,333 --> 01:05:23,533
You mind?

1522
01:05:24,266 --> 01:05:25,700
Not at all.

1523
01:05:27,466 --> 01:05:28,533
What should the caption be?

1524
01:05:31,933 --> 01:05:33,133
Duanduan.

1525
01:05:34,033 --> 01:05:35,233
Duanduan.

1526
01:05:41,333 --> 01:05:42,266
So will you post me?

1527
01:05:44,200 --> 01:05:47,333
If I post, it'll just be...

1528
01:05:49,700 --> 01:05:51,133
The chatterbox.

1529
01:05:51,133 --> 01:05:51,666
Little loudspeaker.

1530
01:05:52,833 --> 01:05:53,533
Big loudspeaker.

1531
01:05:55,400 --> 01:05:55,933
I'll write...

1532
01:05:55,933 --> 01:05:58,600
The loudspeaker that annoys people.

1533
01:05:58,633 --> 01:06:00,866
About sixty percent annoying.

1534
01:06:06,333 --> 01:06:07,533
I'll post it next time we meet.

1535
01:06:08,800 --> 01:06:10,266
Aren't you taking me to dinner?

1536
01:06:10,266 --> 01:06:11,166
I remember.

1537
01:06:13,600 --> 01:06:14,666
Sending it then?

1538
01:06:14,666 --> 01:06:15,866
Alright.

1539
01:06:15,866 --> 01:06:16,300
It's pretty close.

1540
01:06:18,833 --> 01:06:19,300
No.

1541
01:06:20,266 --> 01:06:21,000
No backing out.

1542
01:06:21,033 --> 01:06:23,266
When you're next in Beijing.

1543
01:06:23,266 --> 01:06:25,000
Can I just come immediately?

1544
01:06:25,033 --> 01:06:26,733
Next time you're here,
let's go to Shichahai.

1545
01:06:26,733 --> 01:06:27,666
Can I come right away?

1546
01:06:32,700 --> 01:06:35,033
Right away?

1547
01:06:35,633 --> 01:06:38,033
It's one train ride.

1548
01:06:40,700 --> 01:06:41,566
Up to you.

1549
01:06:41,600 --> 01:06:43,033
Up to me?

1550
01:06:43,033 --> 01:06:43,833
But I'm afraid you would say,

1551
01:06:43,833 --> 01:06:45,133
"Why's this guy so reckless?"

1552
01:06:45,133 --> 01:06:46,433
"Why did he show up?"

1553
01:06:48,000 --> 01:06:49,900
Do whatever you want.

1554
01:07:00,666 --> 01:07:02,500
I've got tons of photos on my phone.

1555
01:07:02,500 --> 01:07:03,500
[Leaning In]
Let me see.

1556
01:07:09,633 --> 01:07:10,900
[Big-head Shark Cosplay]

1557
01:07:10,900 --> 01:07:12,700
[Savage Roast]

1558
01:07:12,700 --> 01:07:14,300
This is hilarious.

1559
01:07:16,200 --> 01:07:17,800
Your face looks thinner than mine.

1560
01:07:17,800 --> 01:07:18,533
Why?

1561
01:07:18,533 --> 01:07:20,433
I have a small face.

1562
01:07:20,466 --> 01:07:21,566
[Self-conscious Now]
No.

1563
01:07:21,600 --> 01:07:23,400
Why?

1564
01:07:23,400 --> 01:07:24,500
I'm closer to the camera.

1565
01:07:24,500 --> 01:07:26,333
Yeah, that tracks.

1566
01:07:26,333 --> 01:07:27,233
[Self-roast Begins]
I look awful in this one.

1567
01:07:27,266 --> 01:07:28,533
[Self-roast Begins]
Don't know why it's so bad.

1568
01:07:28,533 --> 01:07:29,666
It's not.

1569
01:07:29,700 --> 01:07:30,533
It is.

1570
01:07:30,533 --> 01:07:31,666
What are you doing,

1571
01:07:31,700 --> 01:07:32,633
entering a pageant?

1572
01:07:32,666 --> 01:07:33,400
Yeah.

1573
01:07:35,600 --> 01:07:37,400
Why do I look so chubby?

1574
01:07:37,400 --> 01:07:40,033
[Not Happy]
You're not chubby.

1575
01:07:40,033 --> 01:07:41,133
[Complimenting Non-stop]
Stop being ridiculous.

1576
01:07:41,133 --> 01:07:41,866
Not chubby at all.

1577
01:07:41,900 --> 01:07:44,700
[Out of Words]
Where do you even see "chubby"?

1578
01:07:44,700 --> 01:07:46,200
My face looks wide.

1579
01:07:46,233 --> 01:07:46,700
No.

1580
01:07:46,700 --> 01:07:48,333
Isn't that just your face shape?

1581
01:07:48,333 --> 01:07:49,333
This face shape

1582
01:07:49,333 --> 01:07:50,766
looks great with your hairstyle.

1583
01:07:53,033 --> 01:07:55,033
So cute.

1584
01:07:55,033 --> 01:07:56,700
I could look at these all day.

1585
01:07:56,700 --> 01:07:58,033
Yeah. Same.

1586
01:07:59,533 --> 01:08:00,866
I'm so tired.

1587
01:08:00,900 --> 01:08:01,633
Sleep.

1588
01:08:01,666 --> 01:08:03,333
Go to sleep.

1589
01:08:03,333 --> 01:08:05,866
[Here]
Then show me your photos.

1590
01:08:05,900 --> 01:08:07,700
[Admiring the Cute Pics]
I want to see for myself.

1591
01:08:07,700 --> 01:08:10,500
[Hiding from Him]
No, not these.

1592
01:08:10,500 --> 01:08:11,200
[Ugly Pics Deleted Instantly]
You can't look at these.

1593
01:08:11,233 --> 01:08:11,900
Why not?

1594
01:08:13,000 --> 01:08:14,700
[Tough Guy Acting Cute]
Let me see.

1595
01:08:14,700 --> 01:08:15,200
[Denied]
No.

1596
01:08:15,233 --> 01:08:16,333
[Pretty Please]
Please.

1597
01:08:16,333 --> 01:08:17,366
[Cold Rejection]
No.

1598
01:08:17,833 --> 01:08:19,033
[Tough Guy Heartbreak]

1599
01:08:19,033 --> 01:08:20,366
I can send them to you later.

1600
01:08:20,400 --> 01:08:21,266
But you can't look now.

1601
01:08:21,266 --> 01:08:21,966
[Not Even Edited]
None of these are edited.

1602
01:08:24,633 --> 01:08:26,066
You need to protect your image.

1603
01:08:28,666 --> 01:08:29,966
You gaming later?

1604
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:31,333
Gotta place Moonstone votes.

1605
01:08:31,333 --> 01:08:32,166
How'd you vote last night?

1606
01:08:33,266 --> 01:08:34,333
[Not Telling You]
Guess.

1607
01:08:34,333 --> 01:08:36,033
Just tell me.

1608
01:08:36,066 --> 01:08:37,466
Can't reveal votes.

1609
01:08:40,066 --> 01:08:42,066
[Hmph]

1610
01:08:42,066 --> 01:08:43,066
Not saying a thing.

1611
01:08:44,033 --> 01:08:45,466
You never say anything.

1612
01:08:55,900 --> 01:08:57,500
So did you write that note

1613
01:08:57,500 --> 01:08:59,566
yourself?

1614
01:09:00,633 --> 01:09:01,533
[Day nine's secret note:]

1615
01:09:01,533 --> 01:09:02,333
[Got me hooked.
Shouldn't have talked so late.]

1616
01:09:02,333 --> 01:09:04,766
[Slow to warm up and bad at talking,
so all I can do is act and write. - Tao]

1617
01:09:04,800 --> 01:09:06,233
Of course, I wrote it.

1618
01:09:06,233 --> 01:09:08,133
Have you practiced handwriting?

1619
01:09:08,133 --> 01:09:09,266
[Practiced A Bit Just for You]
A little, yeah.

1620
01:09:09,300 --> 01:09:11,033
It's pretty good.

1621
01:09:11,066 --> 01:09:12,466
"Shouldn't have talked so late."

1622
01:09:12,466 --> 01:09:13,800
What does that mean?

1623
01:09:13,833 --> 01:09:15,900
It meant I stayed up too late
talking to you.

1624
01:09:17,100 --> 01:09:18,700
It was around the time

1625
01:09:18,700 --> 01:09:21,166
with Zhang Tianlu

1626
01:09:21,200 --> 01:09:22,666
that we started

1627
01:09:22,666 --> 01:09:24,133
talking more.

1628
01:09:34,933 --> 01:09:36,466
Then I misunderstood.

1629
01:09:36,500 --> 01:09:38,100
I thought you were talking

1630
01:09:38,100 --> 01:09:38,966
to someone else.

1631
01:09:39,000 --> 01:09:41,466
So you wrote my note too late.

1632
01:09:41,466 --> 01:09:42,733
That's what I thought it meant.

1633
01:09:42,733 --> 01:09:44,600
No wonder I didn't get it.

1634
01:09:47,433 --> 01:09:48,700
Silly.

1635
01:09:50,800 --> 01:09:51,600
I was stunned.

1636
01:09:51,600 --> 01:09:53,066
I even read it to Huihui.

1637
01:09:54,033 --> 01:09:54,833
You read it to her?

1638
01:09:55,433 --> 01:09:56,666
I'm done with you.

1639
01:09:57,000 --> 01:09:57,500
What?

1640
01:09:57,500 --> 01:09:58,933
[Inner Monologue]
I can never show my face again.

1641
01:09:58,933 --> 01:09:59,733
[Inner Monologue]
So embarrassing.

1642
01:09:59,733 --> 01:10:01,600
Now you feel like
your writing's terrible?

1643
01:10:01,633 --> 01:10:02,566
So embarrassing.

1644
01:10:02,600 --> 01:10:03,433
Is it that bad?

1645
01:10:03,433 --> 01:10:04,966
Yeah. I'm done.

1646
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:06,233
[Just End Me]

1647
01:10:07,833 --> 01:10:09,033
[Sleepy]

1648
01:10:09,033 --> 01:10:10,266
So tired.

1649
01:10:16,200 --> 01:10:17,000
Sleep.

1650
01:10:18,433 --> 01:10:19,733
If you're tired, sleep.

1651
01:11:03,700 --> 01:11:04,533
What?

1652
01:11:04,533 --> 01:11:05,600
[Caught Red-handed]

1653
01:11:06,100 --> 01:11:07,100
[Trying to Ease the Awkwardness]
Taking a nap?

1654
01:11:07,100 --> 01:11:07,800
[Trying to Ease the Awkwardness]

1655
01:11:09,133 --> 01:11:10,633
I can't help it.

1656
01:11:10,666 --> 01:11:12,166
[Running Out of Energy]

1657
01:11:12,200 --> 01:11:14,633
How long do you usually sleep?

1658
01:11:14,633 --> 01:11:15,666
Usually go to bed at 10:30 p.m.

1659
01:11:15,666 --> 01:11:16,766
and get up at 6:30 a.m.

1660
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:20,133
I admire that.

1661
01:11:20,133 --> 01:11:21,400
But what if sometimes

1662
01:11:21,433 --> 01:11:23,133
friends ask you out

1663
01:11:23,133 --> 01:11:25,433
for drinks or to hang out?

1664
01:11:26,500 --> 01:11:27,600
I don't go.

1665
01:11:27,633 --> 01:11:29,433
[Good Guy Tao]

1666
01:11:29,433 --> 01:11:30,833
Okay.

1667
01:11:30,833 --> 01:11:32,100
Not completely never.

1668
01:11:32,100 --> 01:11:33,333
Most of my friends

1669
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:34,466
don't drink.

1670
01:11:34,500 --> 01:11:35,700
They're all taken anyway.

1671
